1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,067
<i>Remember the guy you videotaped
in the alley?</i>

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,767
<i> Let's prove your loyalty.</i>

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:04,967
<i> Hello, Ramon?</i>

4
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,367
<i> We need to meet here at...</i>

5
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,100
<i> Ramon!</i>

6
00:00:08,233 --> 00:00:10,200
<i> He has injuries on his body,</i>

7
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:11,833
<i>so it looks like he was tortured</i>

8
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,000
<i>before he was completely
silenced.</i>

9
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:15,200
<i>Do you have any idea, Major,
who did this?</i>

10
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,133
<i> Do you know Golda Briones?</i>

11
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:18,567
<i> Stop investigating.</i>

12
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,167
<i> I posted the video on FlipTok.</i>

13
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,867
<i>What if that syndicate
finds you?</i>

14
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,600
<i> I told you earlier</i>

15
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:26,600
<i>that you should have told
your father about this.</i>

16
00:00:26,733 --> 00:00:29,033
<i>Where were you between
1 and 2 AM last night,</i>

17
00:00:29,167 --> 00:00:30,133
<i> Major Delgado?</i>

18
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:31,667
<i>Let's not beat around the bush.</i>

19
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,800
<i> Is he really a hero,</i>

20
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,033
<i>or is he also a member
of the syndicate?</i>

21
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,033
<i>That's the kind of cop
Major Delgado is.</i>

22
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:40,533
<i>A traitor, a crook,
and an immoral person.</i>

23
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:42,967
<i> Your father is fooling us.</i>

24
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,767
Bravo.

25
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,133
Your tirades are solid, Andrew.

26
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:07,167
I'm sure that's trending.

27
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:11,333
One million views in 4 hours.

28
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,667
Wow.

29
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:15,167
That's what I like to hear.

30
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,233
Cheers.

31
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:17,200
Cheers.

32
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,667
So...

33
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,033
this Golda Briones,

34
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:28,633
you are really taking
her word as gospel?

35
00:01:28,767 --> 00:01:31,267
How sure are you that she's not
an asset to the enemy

36
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,400
or just has a personal vendetta
against the cops?

37
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:37,233
She gave me more than words,
Yvette.

38
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:38,867
I have another basis.

39
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,167
What's this?

40
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:48,467
Bank statement of Major
Miguel Delgado.

41
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,467
This was just sent to the studio
by an anonymous source.

42
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:59,267
15 million pesos in one year.

43
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,667
His rank is Major.

44
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,067
Fixed salary.

45
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,467
Even a full colonel won't make
that money in ten years.

46
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,900
So, now, tell me.

47
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:10,967
Where did that come from?

48
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,933
It could be a fabrication,
right?

49
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:17,667
Photoshop or falsified records,
right?

50
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,367
Honey,

51
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,267
Andrew asked me to verify that.

52
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:25,133
So you broke protocol?

53
00:02:25,267 --> 00:02:30,267
And you run with the information
on air, Andrew?

54
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:35,367
Well, the public has the right
to know the truth, Yvette.

55
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,333
You're right, Andrew.

56
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:42,833
The important thing is,
you hit the snake's head.

57
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:47,467
It's easier to squeeze it
before he poisons someone else.

58
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,333
Godfather, thank you for coming.

59
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:03,067
How are you, Joey?

60
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,500
I don't know.

61
00:03:10,933 --> 00:03:12,867
I'm still confused.

62
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,933
But I'm worried more about
mother right now.

63
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:20,933
Do you think father can really
do that?

64
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,800
You know, my child,

65
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:28,200
I've been with your father
for a long time.

66
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,033
He's a good person.

67
00:03:31,867 --> 00:03:33,967
Nobody's perfect, Joey.

68
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:38,700
So sometimes, you can make
mistakes.

69
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,667
What do you mean?

70
00:03:46,133 --> 00:03:50,667
Because once,
Clarissa called me.

71
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,433
<i>Someone called him.
I was the one who answered.</i>

72
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,967
<i> It was a woman's voice.</i>

73
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:57,867
<i>They said they were meeting
in an apartment.</i>

74
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,833
<i> Come on, Clarissa.</i>

75
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:01,133
<i> Maybe she was just a coworker.</i>

76
00:04:01,267 --> 00:04:02,833
<i> No!</i>

77
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:05,533
<i> I have a different feeling.</i>

78
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:07,033
<i> There's a different...</i>

79
00:04:07,167 --> 00:04:09,167
<i>there's a different tone
in the woman's voice.</i>

80
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,600
<i> So, Diego, help me.</i>

81
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,667
<i>Okay, what kind of help
do you need?</i>

82
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:18,800
<i>Find out who that number
belongs to, who owns it.</i>

83
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:23,367
I checked to see who the number
is actually registered to.

84
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,000
Well...

85
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,167
the number is registered
to Golda Briones, my child.

86
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:42,567
Joey, listen to me.

87
00:04:44,333 --> 00:04:47,267
That doesn't mean your father
is a bad person.

88
00:04:50,233 --> 00:04:52,367
Your father was a good cop...

89
00:04:54,133 --> 00:04:56,100
and he is a good father to you.

90
00:04:58,767 --> 00:05:02,400
But in a situation,
there are times really when...

91
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:06,600
there are wrong systems.

92
00:05:06,733 --> 00:05:10,267
And if you're not strong,
you'll be carried away.

93
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:34,233
Godfather.

94
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,300
Let's go.

95
00:05:35,433 --> 00:05:36,333
Let's go inside.

96
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:38,533
<i>Until now, you've been lying,
Miguel.</i>

97
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:39,600
It's mother...

98
00:05:39,733 --> 00:05:41,100
<i> Admit it!</i>

99
00:05:41,233 --> 00:05:42,967
<i> When have you been fooling me?</i>

100
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,067
I'm not fooling you!
I was set up!

101
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,233
And what about that girl?
Is that all?

102
00:05:47,367 --> 00:05:49,600
Is it okay for her
to ruin herself

103
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:52,533
just to make you look bad?
Is that it?

104
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:55,700
Miguel!

105
00:05:56,967 --> 00:05:59,833
I accepted that you were
always gone.

106
00:05:59,967 --> 00:06:01,967
I convinced myself

107
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,900
it was because of your love
for being a policeman.

108
00:06:05,033 --> 00:06:06,833
- That's exactly what it is!
- No!

109
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:08,900
You're a liar!

110
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:13,133
You have a mistress!

111
00:06:13,267 --> 00:06:15,733
That's why you're always gone!

112
00:06:15,867 --> 00:06:20,867
That's why your clothes smell
a different perfume!

113
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,300
That's why someone called you

114
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:25,600
and wanted to meet
at the apartment!

115
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:27,833
Because you're fooling us!

116
00:06:27,967 --> 00:06:30,400
- You're fooling us!
- Mother.

117
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:32,500
You're fooling me!

118
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:53,433
I'm not doing anything wrong,
my child.

119
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,533
Everything they are accusing me
of is a lie.

120
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:19,067
He fooled me, Joey.

121
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:29,133
Your father fooled us.

122
00:07:33,633 --> 00:07:38,167
Mother, maybe we can just listen
to father first.

123
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:40,900
Are you still defending him?

124
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:44,200
Even though he is cheating on us
upfront,

125
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:46,633
will you still take his side?

126
00:07:46,767 --> 00:07:52,400
No, Mother. I just want to hear
father's side.

127
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,433
What side?

128
00:07:57,867 --> 00:08:00,367
What else does he need to do?

129
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:03,900
All throughout our marriage,
that's what I did.

130
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:10,100
He can't come home early.

131
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:13,333
He has a lot of work to finish.

132
00:08:13,467 --> 00:08:15,300
He'll be gone for two days

133
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:17,833
because he's investigating
something.

134
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,600
All of that, Joey...

135
00:08:21,767 --> 00:08:23,833
I accepted all of that.

136
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:31,533
All the love, all the support,
all the understanding,

137
00:08:31,667 --> 00:08:33,567
I gave him.

138
00:08:35,533 --> 00:08:38,667
And then, this is what
he does to us?

139
00:08:46,467 --> 00:08:50,133
Was the love I gave him
not enough?

140
00:08:51,767 --> 00:08:54,500
Was everything I did not enough?

141
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:59,100
What was my fault?
I'll fix it.

142
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:01,367
Nothing, Mother, nothing.

143
00:09:20,667 --> 00:09:22,467
Buddy,

144
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:26,467
just let Clarissa think
for a moment...

145
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,600
so that things will be better.

146
00:09:30,733 --> 00:09:34,000
And as for you, don't neglect
yourself either, okay?

147
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,533
Okay.

148
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,667
Father, we'll go ahead.

149
00:10:23,067 --> 00:10:27,967
Do you also believe
their accusations?

150
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:34,067
I don't want to believe it,
Father, but...

151
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,400
it also made me think
about what the woman said.

152
00:10:39,533 --> 00:10:41,900
The woman you don't know?

153
00:10:43,367 --> 00:10:44,967
Do you believe her more?

154
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:50,700
You probably can't blame me
either, Father.

155
00:10:50,833 --> 00:10:54,167
But I'm ready to listen
to your explanation.

156
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:57,100
What? I need to explain myself
just so you'll believe me?

157
00:10:59,467 --> 00:11:01,167
When I got suspended...

158
00:11:02,333 --> 00:11:04,367
and lost my job

159
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:08,167
because they believed
the accusations against me

160
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:10,000
that aren't true...

161
00:11:12,433 --> 00:11:15,333
I can accept that.
I don't care what they say.

162
00:11:17,133 --> 00:11:19,833
But when my own family turns
their back on me...

163
00:11:50,333 --> 00:11:53,267
So, they're really separated,
right?

164
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,533
I don't know.

165
00:11:59,467 --> 00:12:01,267
Well, maybe there's still
a chance.

166
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,833
You know, I'm sure your father
will find a way

167
00:12:05,967 --> 00:12:07,733
to make your family complete
again. I'm sure.

168
00:12:09,433 --> 00:12:10,800
I hope so, Peter.

169
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:14,900
What do you mean?

170
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:17,333
I know father was hurt too.

171
00:12:18,767 --> 00:12:23,267
I'm sure he thinks mother
and I just abandoned him.

172
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,933
I can't even talk to mother
right now.

173
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,533
You know, this is Andrew's
fault.

174
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:37,000
He doesn't care about the lives
he's destroying

175
00:12:37,133 --> 00:12:39,067
as long as he can post
a video of himself.

176
00:12:40,867 --> 00:12:42,233
Wait.

177
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:43,933
The video.

178
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:46,300
Have you shown your father
the video

179
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,100
of the police officer
who was killed?

180
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:50,667
Not yet.

181
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,600
I forgot about it because
of what happened.

182
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:58,167
Besides, it doesn't look like
anyone is following me.

183
00:12:59,267 --> 00:13:01,700
Maybe I'm just assuming

184
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:04,267
that I'm on the syndicates'
radar.

185
00:13:07,967 --> 00:13:10,033
The videos are really gone,

186
00:13:10,167 --> 00:13:13,167
but only the cameras
in the alley were reset.

187
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,833
The clean-up seems selective.

188
00:13:15,967 --> 00:13:20,967
So that means there's something
they want to hide and erase.

189
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:26,533
So, it's a clear sign
that someone saw me with Ramon,

190
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:30,167
and I want to know
who the hell that was.

191
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,700
Matias, you know I can't be
exposed.

192
00:13:35,833 --> 00:13:37,600
But we also saw something.

193
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:41,033
There's a CCTV that doesn't
belong to the village.

194
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:42,900
They didn't clean it up.

195
00:14:06,367 --> 00:14:07,967
So it's a she.

196
00:14:09,667 --> 00:14:12,700
What we're looking
for is a woman.

197
00:14:18,833 --> 00:14:22,100
Internal Affairs reviewed
your incident report,

198
00:14:22,533 --> 00:14:24,567
as well as the Regional Command.

199
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,467
What did they say, Chief?

200
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,167
Effective immediately,

201
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:32,300
you are placed under preventive
suspension.

202
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:34,233
Pending full investigation.

203
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,900
Dizon's expose didn't help.

204
00:14:39,033 --> 00:14:40,400
There's pressure at the top.

205
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:43,467
Hot item in the intel
and in the media.

206
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,633
It's dangerous if you stay
in the field.

207
00:14:45,767 --> 00:14:48,967
But I'm not like what they say,
Chief.

208
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:52,400
And I believe you,
but I'm not your opponent here.

209
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:53,767
So I advise you,

210
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:57,100
get good legal counsel,
Major Delgado.

211
00:14:58,767 --> 00:15:03,833
But now, you have to surrender
your badge and service firearm.

212
00:15:32,767 --> 00:15:34,367
Permission to leave, Sir.

213
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,467
<i>Can you still handle it?
Jab, jab!</i>

214
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:12,067
<i>Jab. Straight. Uppercut,
uppercut. Jab, jab, jab.</i>

215
00:16:12,233 --> 00:16:13,633
<i> Jab, jab.</i>

216
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:14,400
<i> Straight.</i>

217
00:16:14,533 --> 00:16:15,833
<i> Uppercut.</i>

218
00:16:15,967 --> 00:16:17,133
<i> Ouch, ouch.</i>

219
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:20,133
<i>- Ouch. That's solid.
- Sorry, Father, sorry.</i>

220
00:16:20,267 --> 00:16:23,567
<i>- Timeout, timeout first.
- It's okay. It's just solid.</i>

221
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,500
<i> You know what...</i>

222
00:16:25,633 --> 00:16:27,000
<i>- You're strong.
- Look.</i>

223
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:29,467
<i>Hey, you're tiring your daughter
out. That's enough.</i>

224
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,667
<i> What do you mean?</i>

225
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,167
<i> She can handle that.</i>

226
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:34,000
<i> Right?</i>

227
00:16:34,133 --> 00:16:35,667
<i> By the way, before I forget,</i>

228
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:39,167
<i>I saw a taekwondo class there
at the plaza.</i>

229
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,200
<i>Maybe you want me to enroll you?</i>

230
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:42,300
<i> It's only on weekends.</i>

231
00:16:42,433 --> 00:16:44,500
<i>Well, Father,
do I still need that?</i>

232
00:16:44,633 --> 00:16:47,200
<i>Well, you're right here.
You'll protect us.</i>

233
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:51,633
<i>I won't be here to defend you
forever, right?</i>

234
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:54,767
<i>There will come a time
when you have to fight</i>

235
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,467
<i> even if you don't want to,</i>

236
00:16:56,600 --> 00:17:00,367
<i>especially if you have
to defend yourself.</i>

237
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:05,300
<i>Even if it hurts,
even if it's hard,</i>

238
00:17:05,433 --> 00:17:07,167
<i> you have to fight.</i>

239
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:09,667
<i> Never say die.</i>

240
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:12,433
<i> Never say die.</i>

241
00:17:12,567 --> 00:17:15,433
<i>- What? Training again!
- Okay!</i>

242
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,700
<i>- What, what? Let's eat first.
- Eat. Eat first.</i>

243
00:17:19,867 --> 00:17:22,500
<i>- It's mommy's turn! Mommy!
- You want to get hurt?</i>

244
00:17:22,633 --> 00:17:26,133
<i>- Hurry!
- No!</i>

245
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:34,633
<i>That's the kind of cop
Major Delgado is.</i>

246
00:17:34,767 --> 00:17:39,100
<i>A traitor, a liar,
and an immoral person.</i>

247
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:44,333
This is all your fault,
Andrew Dizon.

248
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,100
Joey, wait! Where are we going?

249
00:17:51,233 --> 00:17:52,167
What's this stuff
we're bringing for?

250
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:53,767
It's so hot!
You didn't even brief me.

251
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:58,133
<i>We are just waiting
for DILG Secretary Mendoza</i>

252
00:17:58,267 --> 00:18:00,367
<i>outside his office
on Mabini Street</i>

253
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:04,167
<i>so we can interview him live
about the case</i>

254
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:06,600
<i> we are focusing on today.</i>

255
00:18:06,733 --> 00:18:09,767
<i>So don't you dare leave,
Ka-Tiradas.</i>

256
00:18:14,267 --> 00:18:15,933
He's already suspended,
Ka-Tiradas.

257
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:22,167
Major Delgado is facing
a lot of civil

258
00:18:22,333 --> 00:18:24,667
and administrative cases.

259
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,333
Well, there's really no place

260
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:30,333
for people like him
in the police force.

261
00:18:30,467 --> 00:18:35,833
He'll only taint their uniforms,
so he deserves it.

262
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:50,567
- Hey, hey! Wait a minute!
- Hey, Andrew Dizon.

263
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,333
Excuse me! Who's this?

264
00:18:53,467 --> 00:18:55,267
What? Are you insulting
the police force again?

265
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:57,467
Are you really not going to stop
with your lies?

266
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:02,867
Look who decided to crawl out
of my screen.

267
00:19:04,367 --> 00:19:05,733
It's JoeyOnDuty.

268
00:19:05,867 --> 00:19:08,700
What brings you here?

269
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:10,833
Why didn't you just bash me
online?

270
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:12,533
I want to do it face-to-face.

271
00:19:12,667 --> 00:19:14,600
Face to face? Why?

272
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,933
Because you know you'll be
embarrassed?

273
00:19:17,067 --> 00:19:20,400
Because you know that everything
I'm exposing is true.

274
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:23,067
Expose your face!

275
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,500
Rotten and trash, that's what
comes out of your mouth.

276
00:19:25,633 --> 00:19:26,867
Do you know that?

277
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,833
Just like your news,
it's rotten.

278
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,767
So this suits you!

279
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:31,900
Joey...

280
00:19:33,567 --> 00:19:36,567
- Hey, wait! Joey!
- Oh my God!

281
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:59,367
What, Buddy?
You're too embarrassed to laugh.

282
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:01,433
Go ahead, laugh.
Start teasing me.

283
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,500
Tell me your friend is a loser.

284
00:20:03,633 --> 00:20:04,400
That's fine.

285
00:20:04,533 --> 00:20:05,700
It seems you hit something
somehow.

286
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:11,167
You know, Buddy, I just wanted
to tell you something.

287
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:13,300
When we were still
at the Academy,

288
00:20:13,433 --> 00:20:14,667
I don't know
if you noticed this.

289
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,467
I was already annoyed with you.

290
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:22,167
Yes, because I know the time
will come...

291
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,400
when you will surpass me
in everything.

292
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:28,400
When it comes to firing,
shooting skills, strategy,

293
00:20:28,533 --> 00:20:30,633
and leadership, right?

294
00:20:30,767 --> 00:20:32,500
Yes.

295
00:20:32,633 --> 00:20:35,967
But you know, I have already
prepared for that, Man.

296
00:20:36,133 --> 00:20:38,167
All I did was strategize.

297
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:40,000
I said I would be close to you.

298
00:20:40,133 --> 00:20:42,033
I will make you my best friend.

299
00:20:42,167 --> 00:20:46,233
So that when the day comes
when we are both in service,

300
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:47,967
your position will be great.

301
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,467
You will be promoted.

302
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,333
And when you got promoted,
man...

303
00:20:53,767 --> 00:20:55,667
I'd be included too,
I'd benefit.

304
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:58,200
And it happened, didn't it?

305
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:01,367
Well, look where my dedication
has taken me.

306
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:07,733
What's with you, Buddy?

307
00:21:09,733 --> 00:21:14,833
The truth will come out
that you are innocent.

308
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:19,200
Just keep on fighting, Buddy.

309
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,300
Just remember,
if you need anything...

310
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:28,167
just say it.
I will do it for you.

311
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:29,333
Thank you.

312
00:21:29,467 --> 00:21:30,633
That's fine.

313
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:32,967
What you're doing for my wife
and daughter is enough.

314
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,467
Thank you very much.

315
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,267
That's what you deserve
for all your slander

316
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,767
against Major Delgado!

317
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:39,400
Sir, I'm sorry.

318
00:21:39,533 --> 00:21:40,800
She went through.

319
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,167
Sir, it's okay.

320
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:45,000
Why?

321
00:21:45,133 --> 00:21:47,667
What do you know about
that police officer?

322
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:51,267
And what do you know about
the case he's handling?

323
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:54,133
I don't know anything
about his case.

324
00:21:54,267 --> 00:21:55,700
But I know my father,

325
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:58,067
and he would never do the things
you're accusing him of!

326
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,300
Wait...

327
00:21:59,433 --> 00:22:02,067
Major Delgado is your father?

328
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,933
Well, no wonder you're defending
the police so much,

329
00:22:05,067 --> 00:22:06,800
you're biased.

330
00:22:06,933 --> 00:22:08,600
I'm not biased!

331
00:22:08,733 --> 00:22:09,800
You're the one!

332
00:22:09,933 --> 00:22:12,367
It's easy for you to say
that my father is a bad person.

333
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:15,300
Because you hate the police!
You're the biased one!

334
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:18,167
The way you act,

335
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:21,067
you think you're a respectable
reporter, right?

336
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:22,633
Why don't you prove it?

337
00:22:22,767 --> 00:22:25,567
Instead of all you do is talk
and fool others!

338
00:22:26,967 --> 00:22:28,600
Well, if you think about it,

339
00:22:28,733 --> 00:22:31,967
you don't care about the lives
of the people you're destroying.

340
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:34,233
You only think about yourself!

341
00:22:36,067 --> 00:22:37,267
Yes,

342
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,233
you're smart,

343
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:41,233
but that's all you have.

344
00:22:41,367 --> 00:22:44,333
You have the brains,
but you have no heart!

345
00:23:07,467 --> 00:23:09,633
Maybe we can increase
mommy's dosage.

346
00:23:09,767 --> 00:23:10,700
Andrew, no!

347
00:23:10,833 --> 00:23:11,833
Get out of this room

348
00:23:11,967 --> 00:23:13,767
if you don't want to give me
my medicine!

349
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:16,167
Has Loloy got an update on
what I'm asking him to find?

350
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:18,633
I told him we should ask
for help.

351
00:23:18,767 --> 00:23:19,500
He said it's not possible

352
00:23:19,633 --> 00:23:21,467
because the police
might kill him.

353
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,333
Is Miguel Delgado the one
he's referring to?

354
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:25,467
The life of a suspended
officer is pretty good,

355
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:26,467
isn't it?

356
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:31,233
Maybe what they're accusing him
of is true.

357
00:23:31,367 --> 00:23:32,433
Just a little patience,

358
00:23:32,567 --> 00:23:34,400
and we'll be able to track down
that woman.

359
00:23:34,533 --> 00:23:36,433
I can't wait to meet her
face-to-face

360
00:23:36,567 --> 00:23:40,267
because she messed
with the wrong person.
